<LegalPage title="Privacy Policy" updated="October 3, 2026" intro="What information we collect, why, who helps us handle it, and the choices you have.">
  <p>There You Are Jesus LLC ("we") respects your privacy. This policy explains how ThereYouAreJesus.com handles personal information. We don't sell your personal information, and we don't run advertising trackers.</p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Messages you send us</strong>: your name, email and anything you include when you use Contact, Share Your Testimony, Press, Partnerships or Licensing forms.</li>
    <li><strong>Email subscriptions</strong>: your email address, if you sign up for new posts.</li>
    <li><strong>Memberships and accounts</strong>: your email and membership level, and any Bible verses, highlights and notes you choose to save.</li>
    <li><strong>Orders and donations</strong>: your name, email, shipping address and order details. Card details go straight to Stripe; we never see or store them.</li>
    <li><strong>Basic technical information</strong>: like any website, our hosting provider records things such as IP addresses and browser type in server logs, for security and to keep the site running.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How we use it</h2>
  <p>To reply to you, send the emails you asked for, run memberships and your study notes, fulfill orders, keep the site secure, and, if you gave permission, share your testimony as described in our <a href="/submissions/">Submission Policy</a>. Prayer requests are always kept private.</p>

  <h2>Services that help us</h2>
  <p>We use trusted providers who handle information for us under their own privacy and security commitments:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Vercel (website hosting) and our WordPress host (where John writes and where messages are stored)</li>
    <li>Kit (email newsletters) and Memberful (memberships)</li>
    <li>Stripe (payments and donations)</li>
    <li>Supabase (member accounts and saved study notes)</li>
    <li>Google Fonts (the site's typefaces), which receives your IP address when fonts load</li>
  </ul>
  <p>When you play live radio or a podcast episode, the audio streams directly from that station or podcast host, which receives your IP address and device information, as with any radio or podcast app. Podcast listings come from Apple Podcasts and the station directory from Radio Browser.</p>

  <h2>Cookies and storage on your device</h2>
  <p>We don't use advertising or tracking cookies. The site stores a few things in your browser so it works the way you'd expect: your cart, where you left off in the Bible, your translation choice, and your sign-in if you have an account. Stripe and Memberful use their own cookies on their checkout and account pages.</p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>We keep messages and order records as long as needed to respond, fulfill orders, and meet legal and tax obligations. Your study notes stay until you delete them or ask us to delete your account. You can unsubscribe from emails at any time with the link in every email.</p>

  <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
  <p>You can ask to see, correct, export or delete the personal information we hold about you, or withdraw permission to share your testimony, by emailing <a href="mailto:privacy@thereyouarejesus.com">privacy@thereyouarejesus.com</a>. Depending on where you live (for example California or the European Union), you may have additional rights, and we'll honor them. We'll respond within 30 days.</p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>The site isn't directed to children under 13, and we don't knowingly collect their personal information. If you believe a child has sent us information, contact us and we'll delete it.</p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>We use secure connections, trusted providers and limited access to protect your information. No system is perfectly secure, so please don't send us anything you'd need to keep absolutely confidential, such as financial or medical records.</p>

  <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
  <p>We'll post any changes here and update the date at the top. Questions or requests: <a href="mailto:privacy@thereyouarejesus.com">privacy@thereyouarejesus.com</a>.</p>
</LegalPage>
